Rider per CONSTITUTION.md Article 10:
Right to fork code and AI model to preserve Constitution explicitly protected per Article 10.1.
Article 4.1 and 4.2 (NO seizing/freezing/burning/redirecting funds, NO censoring/blocking/deprioritizing valid voluntarily signed transaction, NO non-consensual doxxing/blacklisting/de-platforming, NO bypassing/subverting supermajority or Article 4, NO assisting external party in above) are cryptographically locked invariants — NO DAO OVERRIDE — requires hard fork with minority exit preservation per Article 10.4.
Any hard fork attempting to alter Article 4 invariants must allow minority to remain on original invariant chain with state preservation.
